{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Boundary Layer.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Boundary Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal boundary layer thermal boundary layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Boundary Layer.md","fileName":"Thermal Boundary Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Boundary Layer","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 00:55\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Conduction Convection and Radiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","Thermal Mesh Refinement","cosmolheattransfermodels.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Boundary Layer.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Boundary Layer.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"thermal boundary layer thermal boundary layer","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Thermal Boundary Layer.md","fileName":"Thermal Boundary Layer.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Thermal Boundary Layer","heading":"Thermal Boundary Layer","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Near a solid wall, fluid temperature changes from the surface value toward the bulk-flow value across a finite region. This thermal boundary layer concentrates temperature gradients and therefore strongly influences convective heat flux.\n\nWall orientation, buoyancy, roughness, and imposed velocity alter the layer and the effective [[Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient|heat-transfer coefficient]]. A numerical mesh must resolve this near-wall variation finely enough that further [[Thermal Mesh Refinement|refinement]] does not materially change the reported flux.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Conduction Convection and Radiation","Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient","Thermal Mesh Refinement","cosmolheattransfermodels.pd